---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { PROFILE } from '../data/profile';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookies and analytics"
  description="The current cookie status of ORIZ.IN, the local storage keys the site uses, and the optional analytics and advertising integrations."
  lastUpdated="25 October 2026"
>
  <h2>Current status</h2>
  <p>
    ORIZ.IN’s application does not set first-party analytics or advertising
    cookies. Optional Google Analytics 4, Microsoft Clarity, and Google AdSense
    integrations are not loaded unless the operator configures valid identifiers
    and explicitly enables them. At the time of this update, they are disabled.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable data table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Key</th>
          <th scope="col">Type</th>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Lifetime</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>oriz-theme</code></td>
          <td>localStorage</td>
          <td>Remembers an explicit light or dark theme choice.</td>
          <td>Until you clear site data.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>oriz-path:&lt;slug&gt;</code></td>
          <td>localStorage</td>
          <td>Remembers which learning-path steps you marked complete.</td>
          <td>Until you clear site data.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    These values are not sent to ORIZ.IN by the application. You can remove
    them through your browser’s site-data or storage settings. Clearing them
    resets your theme and any learning progress.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare may set security or performance-related cookies as the hosting
    provider, independent of ORIZ.IN’s application code. Cloudflare’s own
    policies and cookie documentation describe those technologies.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
  <p>
    If Google Analytics 4 is enabled, page views may be measured using Google’s
    scripts and identifiers. If Microsoft Clarity is enabled, it may record
    session interactions such as clicks and scrolling outside the masked tool
    areas. Tool interfaces carry a masking attribute, and no tool input values
    are intentionally sent as analytics events. These services set their own
    cookies or identifiers and are governed by their own policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Enabling optional analytics requires appropriate notice and, in some
    jurisdictions, prior consent. The presence of a browser setting is not by
    itself proof of legal compliance, and ORIZ.IN does not claim that it is.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is disabled unless configured. If enabled after approval,
    Google and its partners may use cookies or similar identifiers to serve,
    measure, and limit ads. Those technologies are controlled by Google and are
    subject to the user’s consent choices and regional requirements. Ads are
    labelled and kept separate from tool controls and primary content.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Buy Me a Coffee, GitHub, social platforms, and third-party API
    documentation are external sites. Opening them may create cookies or
    identifiers under their policies. ORIZ.IN does not control those settings.
  </p>

  <h2>How to control cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use your browser’s privacy or site-data settings to block or clear cookies and localStorage.</li>
    <li>Use a content blocker or privacy extension if you want additional control over third-party scripts.</li>
    <li>If optional services are enabled later, use their consent controls or opt-out mechanisms where available.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about storage or tracking:
    <a href={`mailto:${PROFILE.email}?subject=Cookies%20and%20analytics`}>{PROFILE.email}</a>.
    See also the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
